Provenance of the hermo protocol fixtures (recorded 2026-09-11, Hermes v0.21.1,
upstream 2ddeba9e, on this dev box).

events.jsonl
  Recorded live over a loopback gateway (hermes serve on 127.0.0.1, loopback
  bind, legacy ?token= auth) with scripts/record_fixture.py. All frames are
  inbound JSON-RPC exactly as received, one object per line. No session token,
  cookie or Authorization header is present in the file (verified by scanning
  for the token value itself).

  Scenario coverage, in order:
    1. gateway.ready + session.create (result) + session.info — plain turn
    2. message.start/delta/complete — "reply with exactly this sentence"
    3. tool.generating/start/complete + message.complete — shell
       `echo hermo-fixture-tool-check` turn
    4. clarify.request (single-question shape) + session.info mid-clarify —
       clarify answered via clarify.respond with a question_id
    5. busy submit: the result of a second prompt.submit ~2 s into a running
       turn is {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":"r-busy","result":{"status":"redirected"}}
       — this is the verified busy-reply shape on v0.21.1 (PLAN.md §1.3 said
       "session busy"; the wire says status=redirected).

  Not reproducible live: approval.request. This host's agent config runs
  approval_mode="smart" with yolo=false, and the recorded read-only shell
  command auto-allowed, so no approval.request ever hit the wire. Forcing one
  would have required a non-innocuous command. The shape is synthesised in
  events_synthetic.jsonl from PLAN.md §1.4 (verified field list: request_id,
  command (already redacted server-side), description, choices
  ["once","session","always","deny"] subset, smart_denied, allow_session,
  allow_permanent).

  Environment-derived payload warning: session.info carries the live agent's
  system_prompt, skills list and mcp_servers status recorded from the loopback
  capture. These are chat frames required by the reducer (T4), not credentials,
  but anyone re-recording should expect the same fields.

events_synthetic.jsonl
  Lines 1-2: approval.request frames hand-built to the PLAN.md §1.4 shape —
  there is no live capture because the host auto-allowed the recorded tools.
  session_id "SYNTH" is a placeholder; nothing else is synthetic in the real
  file.